   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the state cemetery board to accept from the\ntown of Clarkstown an application for funding from the state cemetery\nvandalism restoration, monument repair or removal and administration fund for\nthree abandoned cemeteries",
    "basePrintNo": "S6878",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6878-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6878\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the state cemetery board to accept\nfrom the town of Clarkstown an application for funding from the state\ncemetery vandalism restoration, monument repair or removal and adminis-\ntration fund for three abandoned cemeteries\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow the Town of Clarkstown to apply for funding established pursu-\nant to section 97-r of the state finance law for maintenance of the\nthree enumerated cemeteries.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill states, notwithstanding any provision of law,\nrule or regulation to the contrary, the state cemetery board is hereby\nauthorized to accept from the town of Clarkstown, Rockland County, an\napplication for funding from the State Cemetery Vandalism Restoration,\nMonument Repair or Removal and Administration Fund established pursuant\nto section 97-r of the state finance law for the maintenance of the\nfollowing abandoned cemeteries: the Nyack Rural Cemetery and the Mount\nMoor Cemetery, both located in West Nyack, and the Nanuet Cemetery,\nlocated in Nanuet.\n\nSection 2 of the bill states that this act shall take effect immediate-\nly.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill seeks to allow the Town of Clarkstown to access funding avail-\nable, under section 97-r of the state finance law, for the maintenance\nof three abandoned cemeteries within its municipality.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
